v4.17.32 — 2026-10-26

On the story card's map, the chapter you came from shows whole above the current one when there is room, instead of with its
first line cut at the card's top edge. Reading guides split a few more lines by language: short English sentences after the
Chinese ("线性。 Linear.", "A single task."), and lines where a script name ends the Chinese sentence before the English starts.

v4.17.31 — 2026-10-26

The mandate chapters no longer end on an empty "Reward:" (the reward was a game value the archive cannot show); in guides,
a bold range of documents with one name ("2030–2037 伦理变化") keeps both its links instead of tying the name to the last one.

v4.17.30 — 2026-10-26

The story map names things with each chapter's own reviewed names: labels that read "这个名字" / "this name" (the
Marauders' map had 32) now say what the chapter says. Only interchangeable outcomes merge into one card (conditional branches
into one story stay separate cards with their own conditions). The line under a guide's title splits by language only where it
is written plainly, and stays whole otherwise. In guides, a bold "id name" ("2006 宗教狂热") becomes one link in the guide's
own words instead of "宗教狂热宗教狂热", and a name repeated in brackets after a link is dropped. A chapter with many versions
of its text that are partly named offers them in one "Version" menu instead of a row of fifteen tabs.

v4.17.29 — 2026-10-26

From a second reading of random stories: where many possible outcomes lead into one other story (a dig's 38 possible
incidents), they read as one card, "one of 38 chapters", with their combined chance, instead of 38 identical cards; very
small chances read "<1%" instead of "0%". The line under each reading guide's title ("Category · DLC") shows only the page's
own language. An astral rift no longer repeats its name as its only text. Long script paths in guides wrap on phones; a guide
line whose English opens with a quote ("'Deal' or 'No deal'") is split by language; the effects panel no longer prefixes a line
with the word it starts with ("Leader · Leader experience +200").

v4.17.28 — 2026-10-26

Corrections from a review of the last three releases: a chapter whose text is one composed description (an introduction, then
its list of boons or factions) reads in order again instead of being split into versions (ten chapters, one of which showed an
empty version); the gameplay-effects panel keeps every random option (three equal 33% outcomes are three again) and every
different effect that shares a wording (a "+3" minerals and a "+3" energy deposit are two again), and repeats of one effect
read "×2"; an option is marked "Always shown" or "Always available" only when it truly has no condition, and where some
options have conditions that cannot be named the shared line says "Most of these appear only when: …".

v4.17.27 — 2026-10-26

Chapters whose game text comes in several versions with no recorded condition (a storm of eight kinds, a faction's six
replies: 177 chapters) show one version at a time with a small "Version 1 2 3 …" row, instead of running them together as one
narrative. Reading guides keep to one language better: items written in only one language stay on their own page (they showed
on both), a guide written only in Chinese shows whole on the English page instead of bare headings, script names are no longer
cut off as a line's "English" ("has_shroud_dlc）。"), and where one paragraph links several chapters that share a title (the
steps of one anomaly) the links keep the guide's numbers instead of repeating the title. The gameplay-effects panel no longer
says the same line twice (a game tooltip and the effect it describes, a condition inside the same condition); the same effect
from two script lines reads once with "×2".

v4.17.26 — 2026-10-26

A requirement that a list of choices shares is said once too ("Unless marked, these require: …"), with the options it does not
apply to marked "Always available"; an option whose condition has no readable name is no longer marked "Always shown". Five
chapters no longer end a paragraph with "If: other conditions ERROR", the game's own placeholder for a case it never reaches.

v4.17.25 — 2026-10-26

Long lists of choices read cleaner: a condition that every option shares, or nearly every one, is said once under "Your
choices" instead of under each option (the Shroud's 49 boons each carried "Only when: earlier events"); the few options it does
not cover are marked ("Always shown", or their own condition). Conditions built from several unnamed game flags no longer read
as nonsense ("Only when: not earlier events or earlier events" is now "Only when: earlier events").

v4.17.24 — 2026-10-26

On phones and tablets the music bar's knob no longer sits alone on the screen's edge as a gold dot before anything has played;
it appears once a piece plays or has begun. On a tablet held upright the story card's map bar no longer shows its chapter count
cut mid-word ("74 cha…"): where the bar is too narrow the count steps aside, as it already did on short screens. In English
guides, a note kept in brackets after a linked name keeps its space ("“Reprise” (the second leader)").

v4.17.23 — 2026-10-26

Reading guides, the other half of the echo: where a guide writes a chapter's name and then its id ("**Diamond in the Rough**
(4055):", "大召唤（2021）", "“交织的喜悦”（336，组织者想留下）"), the written name itself now opens the chapter and the id goes,
instead of reading "Diamond in the Rough (Diamond in the Rough):" (about 870 places, both languages).

v4.17.22 — 2026-10-26

Reading guides stop saying a chapter's name twice: where a guide named an event by its id and then its quoted title, the id
already reads as that title, so the quote went ("The Gray Tempest "The Gray Tempest": …" is now "The Gray Tempest: …"; about
2,000 places across the guides, both languages). A speck beside the top bar (a disclosure arrow's tip scrolling under it) is gone.

v4.17.21 — 2026-10-26

Search results read better: a chapter found by its title no longer repeats that title as its excerpt ("Rift Manifestation ·
…" over "Rift Manifestation"); it shows where the words occur in the chapter, or its opening lines. Excerpts keep to two lines
as intended (some ran to five), and start at a sentence or a word instead of a stray full stop ("…。这些粒子…").

