v4.11.0 — 2026-10-26

Finishing touches. English is typeset — curly quotes and apostrophes, real dashes and ellipses — without changing a word
of the game's text; warning lines such as "-Warning: Challenging origin" stand on their own line. Stories without a
picture get a typographic slate in the page's language instead of a blank panel. A newcomer sees one line saying what the
archive is; the graphics notice folds into a small chip. The panels at the foot of a chapter share one style; reviewer
notes are folded away. The Grand Archive fits English phones; map captions break at words; the trigger eyebrow no longer
repeats itself.

v4.10.0 — 2026-10-26

Editorial pass on everything around the text. Choices are a ruled list in the text's own measure; the chosen one opens
its answer beneath it. Conditions name only what is known (no more "other conditions"), random outcomes sit under one
bracket with their chances, and cards that every choice leads to are listed once. Endings are set centred with the next
story as its own card; Back, "From …" and Start over share one quiet line above the title. The archive's selection panel
reads as one ruled column with the reading progress in it; the category bar no longer clips; the Grand Archive has a
plaque-style header, text tabs for filters and exhibit effects set as a table; search stays anchored and shows focus.

v4.9.0 — 2026-10-26

Reads like a book. Paragraphs are set with measured breaks instead of empty lines, Chinese text is justified with
compressed punctuation, and titles use proportional punctuation. The Chinese typefaces are now served by the site itself
(Noto Serif SC and Noto Sans SC, in the intended weights), so they look the same everywhere and load in a third of the
bytes. The story map opens full-size with two-line chapters, a complete legend and an overview of even the largest
stories; repeated branches are merged. Story guides read as companion essays. Effects and search labels are quieter. On
phones the reader's header is compact, the Grand Archive's exhibits have their own history step (Back closes the exhibit
first), and landscape phones get far more reading space.

v4.8.0 — 2026-10-19

Smoother first opening: a story opened from the archive now appears in a single frame in most cases, and its map fills in
quietly around the current chapter. The archive remembers what you have read ("3 of 12 read"), and the Grand Archive
marks specimens you have met while reading, with a filter for them. Number keys 1–9 pick a choice or continue card.
Story guides read in chapter titles instead of event numbers — each title opens its chapter — and no longer hide part of
their Chinese text; editor notes, sources and empty sections are folded away, and five guides gained their English half.
Search finds words as you type them (prefixes), single Chinese characters and near-misses ("Close matches"). Plainer
wording across effects and the interface (an AI proofread pass in both languages), better screen-reader names, contrast
and touch targets, and two re-generated specimen models (Sniran Spikes, Gargantua Megalus).

