v4.4.0 — 2026-10-15

Every sentence with a name the game fills in was read again as the site shows it and corrected where it read
unnaturally (articles, titles, pronouns, repeated nouns, computed values); scripted passages that showed nothing
now show the game's own words. The effects panels now itemise every effect the game files contain, give all
origins their starting effects and drawbacks, and read in natural Chinese and English throughout.

v4.3.0 — 2026-10-15

Sharper art: event pictures and specimen icons have super-resolved versions (Real-ESRGAN, originals kept) for
close-ups and high-density screens. Each choice, document and origin now has an optional, collapsed panel with its
gameplay effects as read from the game files — rewards, costs, modifiers and durations, chances and conditions —
without simulating a save. Names the game fills in read more naturally, including inside scripted passages and game
terms. Calmer interface: fewer hints and labels, consistent spacing, quicker transitions.

v4.2.0 — 2026-10-15

Refinement. Story guides are formatted (headings, lists, quotes, links) and show the reading language first.
Dragging the story map no longer selects page text. Names the game fills in from a save now read as natural phrases
("our science ship", "the other empire") chosen per story in complete sentences, with a short explanation on hover,
focus or tap; the original text is kept. New typography (Newsreader, Noto Serif SC, Noto Sans SC), the site is
simply "Stellaris Tales", the Grand Archive sits in the main navigation, and the soundtrack starts with Faster Than
Light (vocal) when the browser allows it, or on the first click.

v4.1.1 — 2026-10-14

Grand Archive: opening the museum while the site was still starting (or from a #museum link) could build the
exhibit hall twice and list every specimen twice; it is now built once.

v4.1.0 — 2026-10-14

博物天枢 · Grand Archive museum: all 258 specimens from the game files (base game and installed DLC) with original
icons, bilingual names and descriptions, exhibit effects with their conditions, how each is acquired and links to the
story documents that award it (and back). Every specimen has a rotatable, zoomable 3D model: an unofficial AI
reconstruction from the game icon (unseen sides are guesses, not canonical), loaded on demand with the original image
as fallback. GPU tiers prefer the discrete GPU and lighten rendering on integrated adapters.

v4.0.2 — 2026-10-13

Review records completed and audited: every story has a reviewed fragment and a guide with all five sections that
cites the game files (event-leviathans-98 gained its guide; 63 guides gained missing sections). The two unused
developer test event chains are no longer listed (1,388 stories, 8,668 documents).

v4.0.1 — 2026-10-13

Smoother reading: the story map on the left card is built after the extracted card settles when a story opens,
and in the next idle period after a chapter change, so it no longer shares a frame with the new text (worst frame
on open 100-112 ms -> 76-82 ms, chapter change 58-82 -> 41 ms, back 17-41 -> 12 ms on an RTX 5070 Laptop).
Reader checks now include cross-story reading-context consistency.

v4.0.0 — 2026-10-13

Stellaris Tales V4: story trees for every story in the local Stellaris installation (base game and installed DLC
files). 1,390 reviewed stories in eight categories (acceptance evidence in content/chronology/REVIEW.md), 8,670
original bilingual documents, event inheritance resolved, a source-grounded guide per story, GPU archive scene and
Detroit-style flow map. Changing this file on main publishes the site (see docs/RUNBOOK.md, "Release").
